<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.3.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01624</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.3.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d8dddaa6-bf4d-4792-9923-3704da452c4f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson. Double click on mathematical expressions/equations to enlarge.</para>

<para>For questions 1 - 2, find the quotients using division.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section><exercise id="af56f7e8-d1e7-434e-b3eb-e09a0a5bd450" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(\frac{45x^5y^9}{-60x^8y^6}\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(-\frac{3x^3}{4y^3}\)</para><para>\(-\frac{4y^3}{3x^3}\)</para><para>\(-\frac{3y^3}{4x^3}\)</para><para>\(-\frac{3}{4}x^3y^3\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.3.1. 
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(-\frac{3y^3}{4x^3}\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_3bf78ebd-82c8-4f1f-8b4c-05ee2395ef08" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((48y-24x) \div (2y-x)\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(24\)</para><para>\(-24x\)</para><para>\(24y\)</para><para>\(-24\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.3.1.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(24\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_8c897ca2-721c-4794-b080-53466399c4be" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For questions 3 and 4, divide using long division.</para><para>\((m^3+1000) \div (m+10)\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(m^2+10m\)</para><para>\( m^2-100\)</para><para>\(m^2+10m-100\)</para><para>\(m^2-10m+100\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.3.2.</para><para>The correct answer is \(m^2-10m+100\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="da27cc16-8c18-479e-ae6f-af78cd8f76c1" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((125y^3-64) \div (5y+4)\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(25y^2-20y+16- \frac{128}{5y+4}\)</para><para>\(25y^2-20y+16- \frac{64}{5y+4}\)</para><para>\(25y^2+20y+16\)</para><para>\(25y^2-20y+16\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.3.2.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(25y^2-20y+16- \frac{128}{5y+4}\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="bf202dfc-071e-44eb-ab0e-101d9a6c3441" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For questions 5 - 6, divide using synthetic division.</para><para>\((b^3-3b^2-4b+12) \div (b+2)\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(b^2+5b\); remainder \(6\)</para><para>\( b^2-5b+6\); remainder \(0\)</para><para>\(b^2-5b\); remainder \(6\)</para><para>\(b^2+5b-6\); remainder \(0\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.3.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \( b^2-5b+6\); remainder \(0\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_348c050e-ab7c-4194-ba9c-dc70001ba540" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((3x^4-11x^3+2x^2+10x+6) \div (x-3)\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(3x^3+2x^2+4x+2\); remainder \(0\)</para><para>\(3x^3-20x^2-62x-180\); remainder \(0\)</para><para>\(3x^3-2x^2-4x-2\); remainder \(0\)</para><para>\(3x^3-2x^2-4x\); remainder \(-2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.3.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(3x^3-2x^2-4x-2\); remainder \(0\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_22d7851a-2f27-4df6-8c77-1829103c897a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For questions 7 and 8, use the following polynomial functions.</para><para>\(f(x)=x^2-13x+36\)
       </para>
        <para>\(g(x)=x-4\)</para>
      <para>Find \((\frac{f}{g})(x)\).</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x+9\)</para><para>\(x-12\)</para><para>\(x-3\)</para><para>\(x-9\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.3.4. 
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(x-9\).

     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="bc2aeeea-7d9b-4b1b-9759-b1227a6756df" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Find \((\frac{f}{g})(-1)\).</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(-8\)</para><para>\( -10\)</para>
      <para>\( -4\)</para><para>\( 8\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.3.4.</para><para>The correct answer is –10.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_932f9bd3-9a6c-4230-9522-bcfc683c8ce7" class="multiple-choice"><problem>
        <para>Use the Remainder Theorem to find the remainder.</para>
          <para>\(f(x)=x^2-4x-9\) is divided by \(x + 2\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>3</para><para>21</para><para>-13</para><para>-9</para>
    </problem>
    <solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.3.5.</para><para>The correct answer is 3.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="ef170a4b-4c96-4a7e-9036-fcf0b2a55c3a" class="multiple-choice"><problem>
        <para>Use the Factor Theorem to determine if \(x-3\) is a factor of \(x^3-7x^2+11x+3\).
       </para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>Yes</para><para>No</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.3.5.
     </para><para>The correct answer is yes.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
